Description: End an element that is never closed where its content ends
 An element closed by an ancestor's close tag (EHP-07), or left open at the
 end of the input, kept the range and location of its open tag while its
 children ran past it. ESLint's getNodeByRangeIndex then skipped the whole
 subtree and getText returned only the open tag. Such an element now ends
 where its last child ends; one with no children still ends at its open tag.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("ends elements that an ancestor's close tag closes where their content ends", "ends elements left open at the end of the file where their content ends"); the "child inside parent" output check now covers unclosed elements; upstream snapshot "Custom tag raw content" updated: the element left open inside <markdown> now ends with its text
Last-Update: 2026-10-19
